    "workedSolution": "1. 2 women and 3 men: $6 \\times 20 = 120$; 3 women and 2 men: $4 \\times 15 = 60$; 4 women and 1 man: $1 \\times 6 = 6$. Total $186$. ($336$ chooses 2 women then any 3 others, which counts some teams more than once.)"
   }
