       "id": "p",
       "input": "number"
      },
      {
       "id": "q",
       "input": "number"
      }
     ]
    },
    "answerSpec": {
     "blanks": [
      {
       "id": "p",
       "accepted": [
        "0.25"
       ],
       "marks": 1,
       "tolerance": 0.0005
      },
      {
       "id": "q",
       "accepted": [
        "0.3"
       ],
       "marks": 2,
       "tolerance": 0.0005
      }
     ]
    },
    "explanation": "$0.2 + p + q + 0.25 = 1$ gives $p + q = 0.55$. $\\mathrm{E}(X) = 0.2 + 2p + 3q + 1 = 2.6$ gives $2p + 3q = 1.4$. Then $q = 1.4 - 2(0.55) = 0.3$ and $p = 0.25$."
   },
   {
    "label": "(b)",
    "type": "NUMERICAL",
    "marks": 3,
    "stem": "Find Var(X).",
    "answerSpec": {
     "value": 1.1400000000000015,
     "tolerance": {
      "kind": "absolute",
      "amount": 0.005
     }
    },
    "explanation": "$\\mathrm{E}(X^2) = 0.2 + 4(0.25) + 9(0.3) + 16(0.25) = 0.2 + 1 + 2.7 + 4 = 7.9$. $\\mathrm{Var}(X) = 7.9 - 2.6^2 = 1.14$.",
    "workedSolution": "1. $\\mathrm{E}(X^2) = 0.2 + 4(0.25) + 9(0.3) + 16(0.25) = 0.2 + 1 + 2.7 + 4 = 7.9$. $\\mathrm{Var}(X) = 7.9 - 2.6^2 = 1.14$."
   }
  ],
  "explanation": "Two equations from ΣP = 1 and E(X), then E(X²) − [E(X)]².",
