  "estimatedSeconds": 720,
  "stem": "A bag contains 6 green and 4 white counters. Farai takes two counters at random from the bag, one after the other, without replacement.",
  "parts": [
   {
    "label": "(a)",
    "type": "NUMERICAL",
    "marks": 2,
    "stem": "Find the probability that the two counters are the same colour. Give your answer as a fraction or a decimal correct to 3 significant figures.",
    "answerSpec": {
     "value": 0.4666666666666667,
     "tolerance": {
      "kind": "absolute",
      "amount": 0.0005
     }
    },
    "explanation": "$\\frac{6}{10} \\times \\frac{5}{9} + \\frac{4}{10} \\times \\frac{3}{9} = \\frac{30 + 12}{90} = \\frac{7}{15}$. (0.52 is $0.6^2 + 0.4^2$, with replacement.)",
    "workedSolution": "1. $\\frac{6}{10} \\times \\frac{5}{9} + \\frac{4}{10} \\times \\frac{3}{9} = \\frac{30 + 12}{90} = \\frac{7}{15}$. (0.52 is $0.6^2 + 0.4^2$, with replacement.)"
   },
   {
    "label": "(b)",
    "type": "NUMERICAL",
    "marks": 2,
    "stem": "Find the probability that the second counter is white.",
    "answerSpec": {
     "value": 0.4,
     "tolerance": {
      "kind": "absolute",
      "amount": 0.0005
     }
    },
    "explanation": "$\\frac{6}{10} \\times \\frac{4}{9} + \\frac{4}{10} \\times \\frac{3}{9} = \\frac{24 + 12}{90} = 0.4$.",
    "workedSolution": "1. $\\frac{6}{10} \\times \\frac{4}{9} + \\frac{4}{10} \\times \\frac{3}{9} = \\frac{24 + 12}{90} = 0.4$."
   },
   {
    "label": "(c)",
    "type": "NUMERICAL",
    "marks": 2,
    "stem": "Given that the two counters are the same colour, find the probability that they are both white. Give your answer as a fraction or a decimal correct to 3 significant figures.",
    "answerSpec": {
